<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ's SBS cuts floating mortgage rate to 9.75 pct.</title>
<headline>NZ's SBS cuts floating mortgage rate to 9.75 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand's Southland Building Society said on Wednesday it had reduced its variable home loan rate to 9.75 percent from 10.5 percent.  </p>
<p>SBS said it had also reduced its fixed rates, with six months fixed now available at 7.95 percent.</p>
<p>The new rates were effective for new borrowers from December 20, and for existing clients from January 27, 1997.</p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
</text>
